# check_refs.py exemptions — one regex per line, '#' starts a comment.
#
# A pattern here says: this target is described in prose but does not exist in
# this repository, and that is correct. Exempting it is a decision, so each
# line carries the reason. Every remaining MISSING is a real defect.
#
# Read by: scripts/check_refs.py (default), .pre-commit-config.yaml, CI.
# Override with --ignore-file '' to see the unexempted list.

# Subproject state files. The Skill contract describes state/*.md; the files
# only exist inside a novel subproject.
^state/

# Setting and character documents quoted as examples in the module contracts.
^worldbuilding/
^characters/
^issues/
^notes-personal/

# README FOR AI.md is written from the subproject's point of view, so its
# paths are relative to a tree this repository does not contain.
^README_FOR_AI_Audit_Report
^filepath$
^(\.\./)+references/
^method-patterns-(worldbuilding|character|chapter|continuity|publishing)\.md$

# CHANGELOG.md quotes the path it used to contain, in the entry announcing the
# fix. It is a historical record, not a live link.
^\.\./CHANGELOG\.md$
